+/*
+ * A control's template (or a UserControl's content) declares visual state groups on its root
+ * (VisualStateManager.VisualStateGroups); VisualStateManager.GoToState looks the state up there, takes
+ * back what the group's previous state set and sets what the new one does: its Setters (Target
+ * "Element.Property", a property path) and the held end values of its Storyboard's animations
+ * (Storyboard.TargetName / TargetProperty: a DoubleAnimation's or ColorAnimation's To, the last key
+ * frame's Value).  These values are a layer above the local values (dobj_set_animated_value), as
+ * animations are on Windows.  Animations are not run over time: a state's look is reached at once,
+ * transitions are not played.  A Storyboard begun from code sets its end values the same way and
+ * reports Completed soon after.  Interface identity per windows-rs 0.30.0 (MIT).
+ */
+
